g, skips heredoc bodies, splits chains on operators outside quotes only, keeps case, and reads `bash -c '\u2026'`, `sh -c`, `cmd /c`, `pwsh -Command` by parsing the inner string recursively; wrappers like `sudo`, `nohup`, `time`, `env` are skipped as leading words. No import from `production_gate.py`.\n\n**spec.md**\n\n6. Requirements, the sandbox block: name `.claude` and `framework` as directories (the sandbox skips a glob on Linux, as the spec itself says), not \"the four guardrail files\". The `ci_settings_file` rewrite is a second rule beside `_ANCHORED_RULE` (`run_phase.py:1067`, which matches `Read|Edit` rules only and would leave a bare path untouched): a `./X` or bare `X` entry under `sandbox.filesystem.denyWrite` becomes the absolute filesystem path `<project root>/X` (the sandbox's own spelling: a leading `/` is absolute; not the `//` permission spelling), the `protected_paths` entries of `sdlc.yaml` are appended the same way and a glob among them is skipped with a note in the result JSON. The test in `tests/test_ci.py` asserts the exact rendered list.\n\n7. Acceptance: rewrite line 243 so the spec itself carries none of the scanner's literals \u2014 the line currently contains `eval(`, `exec(` and `shell=True`, and `check.py`'s `DANGEROUS` patterns read a `.md` in the diff too, so the design diff reports three findings against its own Acceptance. Say \"none of the scanner's three dangerous-call patterns (`check.py`, `DANGEROUS`)\".\n\n8. Requirements: add the sentence item 10 asked for: the scan's classification of an unbounded finding as `feature` (`route.py:468`) is a framework item for 0.3.x, not this change.\n\n9. Acceptance: name the tests of item 6 (the relative-path, `cd`, non-literal cases) here as well as in the plan's Proof; say that a non-literal `cd` with no write after it in the chain is allowed (the hook judges write targets, not directories), and add `2>&1` and `> /dev/null` to the negative list.\n\n**plan.md**\n\n10. Files that change: dr